   "source": "After interpolation, an outlier analysis was performed on each measurement type and time point. Patients that did not have a baseline, T1, or T2 datapoint were not included in the sample for the corresponding measuremnt/change in time. For each sample, the mean and standard deviation were calculated. Then, the z-score of each patient was calculated. For this analysis, outliers were considered to be patients that had a z-score greater than two standard deviations away from the mean. Outliers were then removed from the sample for the final linear regression and mean % change analysis.",
   "id": "c2f847a22e375315"
